      walkthrough = "**Level:** 1\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Solo\n\nThis Erollisi Day task starts with Muku Wolfeetz [npc=60445] in The Overthere (old Kunark zone) at /way -3075, 1932, -48 outside the city walls on the east side.\n(Note: Before starting, make sure you have a fishing pole, you will need for a later step).\nYou say, 'Hail, Muku Wolfeetz'\nMuku Wolfeetz says, 'Hail, _____. The day is long, and the night is too [short]. '\nYou say, 'Are you calling me short?'\nMuku Wolfeetz says, 'Nay, _____. I hate handling my [tasks] in the day, and don't have enough time in the night.  '\nYou say, 'What tasks are you working on?'\nMuku Wolfeetz says, 'I am working on a secret project and am still collecting all of the [supplies] I need.'\nYou say, 'I could collect the supplies you need.'\nMuku Wolfeetz says, 'Why would you want to [help me]? I am not going to reward a Wood Elf. And I am not telling you what I am working on.  '\nYou say, 'Don't  think of it as me helping you. Think of it as you helping me.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Lures Hurt'.\nMuku Wolfeetz says, 'Fine, go collect some bones for me and then we can talk some more. '\nMuku Wolfeetz isn't sure about trusting you. You will need to work on getting his trust before you can ask him about Darenne's missing treats. He has a few tasks that he is willing to have you do for him.\nHead east along the shore and search for an iksar skeleton's bones.\n- 1. Head east past the wreck 0/1 The Overthere\nThis is a location update at /way 3188.33, -1790.69, -24.38 which is straight east of the city.\nOnce you get the location update an iksar skeleton spawns and attacks.\n- 2. Kill the iksar skeleton 0/1 The Overthere\nKill it. You get Iksar Tailbone [item=151173] on your cursor.\n- 3. Return to Muku and talk to him 0/1 The Overthere\nYou say, 'Hail, Muku Wolfeetz'\nMuku Wolfeetz says, 'Hail, ______. Did you get that [iksar tailbone]?'\nYou say, 'Yes. I have a iksar tailbone. Why did you want this thing?'\nMuku Wolfeetz says, 'Well, now. I'm not sure why I would want to tell you that. A guy must have some [secrets].'\nYou say, ' What kind of secrets?'\nMuku Wolfeetz says, 'It is the season of love, and no one ever said what type of love. Maybe I want to do something [nice] for a friend.'\nYou say, 'That does sound nice. Did you need anything else for that friend?'\nMuku Wolfeetz says, 'Hrrm. I do need a part from an [sarnak skeleton].'\nYou say, 'I can get a part from an sarnak skeleton'\nYour task 'Lures Hurt' has been updated.\nMuku Wolfeetz says, 'Head a bit south from where you found the first skeleton. There you should be able to find the next. '\n- 4. Head south from where you found the skeleton 0/1 The Overthere\nThis is a location update at /way 1932, -1657, -42. There is a sarnak skeleton near a boulder at this location. It will attack you, kill it. It drops Sarnak Voicebox [item=151174], loot it.\n- 5. Return to Muku and hail 0/1 The Overthere\nYou say, 'Hail, Muku Wolfeetz'\nYour task 'Lures Hurt' has been updated.\nMuku Wolfeetz says, 'Good to see you again _____. I was worried that I would have to go [save] you. '\nYou say, ' There is no need to save me. Since we are friends now, do you know anything about Darenne missing treats or who took them?'\nYour task 'Lures Hurt' has been updated.\nMuku Wolfeetz says, 'I heard about that, I am not sure who took them, but I was given one as a gift. You help me [finish] my gift and I will give you the one I have. '\nYou say, 'I can help you finish, but I want to know who gave it to you.'\nMuku Wolfeetz says, 'Ha. We aren't that good of friends. Once you find the last two items you can go ahead and can make the lure. I can't wait to see your craftmanship. '\n- 6. Fish up a cockatrice claw 0/1 The Overthere\nFish along the shore, doesn't matter where along the shore. Catch a Cockatrice Claw [item=151175], don't spill your beer in the process.\n....sigh, you spilled your beer didn't you?\n- 7. Collect beach grass 0/1 The Overthere\nBunch of Beach Grass [item=151176] looks like a purple collectible on the ground near /way 3556, 1559, 127. Loot it.\n- 8. Craft the Totem of Love and Ocean 0/1 ALL\nThe Cockatrice Claw is a container. Place the Tailbone, Voicebox and the Bunch of Beach Grass inside the claw and combine to make the Totem of Love and Ocean [item=151177].\n- 9. Deliver the Totem of Love and Ocean 0/1 The Overthere\nReturn to Muku and give him the totem. Squeezed Glee [item=151172] (needed for Only Fools Fall In [quest=13292]) will appear on your cursor.\nYou offered 1 Totem of Love and Ocean to Muku Wolfeetz.\nYou have been given: Squeezed Glee\nYour task 'Lures Hurt' has been updated.\nYou have successfully earned Muku's trust and received the Squeezed Glee drink from him.\nMuku Wolfeetz says, 'Now that is a fine-looking lure. Nice and sharp too. Here you can have this drink. It looks way too sweet for me away. '\nYou complete the trade with Muku Wolfeetz.\nYou are given: Squeezed Glee\nReward(s):\nBox of Scrumpious Sultry Candy Hearts [item=151170] - Converts to - 6x Scrumpious Sultry Candy Heart [item=151169] (Req Level 45: HP: 10, Mana: 10 - Miraculous meal)\nSubmitted by: GidonoRewards:\n- Box of Scrumpious Sassy Candy Hearts [item=151170]\n- Scrumpious Sassy Candy Heart [item=151169]\n[",
